Rem ==================================================================
Rem oregon-core.shoddy — The Oregon Trail, the pure model.
Rem
Rem A port of OREGON (Bill Heinemann, 1971, for MECC) from the
Rem oregon.bas listing in this folder. Everything the game IS that does
Rem not touch the console: the Trail state record, the outfitting and
Rem eating arithmetic, the date table, the fourteen-day travel formula,
Rem the rider encounters, the sixteen-entry misfortune table, the
Rem mountain crossings, and the arrival-date computation. It includes
Rem nothing, so it runs headless and is checked that way (test.shoddy).
Rem oregon.shoddy adds the prompts, the timed shooting, and the turn
Rem loop on top.
Rem
Rem Randomness: any roll that DECIDES a branch (did riders appear, which
Rem misfortune, did the shot miss) arrives as a parameter, so every
Rem branch is reachable deterministically from the tests. Rolls that
Rem only jitter a magnitude (how many miles a breakdown costs) call Rnd
Rem directly, the way invaders-core's RandomAlien does.
Rem
Rem The BASIC's variables map onto Trail fields: M Miles, M2 PrevMiles,
Rem F Food, B Bullets, C Clothing, M1 Misc, T Cash, A Oxen, D3 TurnNo,
Rem E Eating, D9 Skill, K8 Injured, S4 Ill, M9 ShowPass, F1 ClearedPass,
Rem F2 ClearedBlue, X1 FortDue. Death (its GOTO 5170) is the Dead fate.
Rem ==================================================================

Rem ---- tunables ------------------------------------------------------

Def TotalMiles() As Number
    2040

Rem $900 saved less $200 already paid for the wagon.
Def StartBudget() As Number
    700

Def DoctorFee() As Number
    20

Rem Below this much food you are warned, then you starve.
Def LowFood() As Number
    13

Rem Forts charge more: a dollar buys two-thirds of what it did at home.
Def FortRate() As Number
    2 / 3

Rem Hunting or fighting takes more bullets than this.
Def FewBullets() As Number
    39

Rem Shot quality of a botched word — the worst possible shot.
Def MissShot() As Number
    9

Rem ---- state ---------------------------------------------------------

Type Outcome = Rolling | Dead(Msg)

Type Trail
    Miles       As Number       Rem M  - total mileage so far
    PrevMiles   As Number       Rem M2 - mileage at the last turn's start
    Food        As Number       Rem F  - dollars' worth of food
    Bullets     As Number       Rem B  - count, not dollars
    Clothing    As Number       Rem C
    Misc        As Number       Rem M1 - medicine and repairs
    Cash        As Number       Rem T
    Oxen        As Number       Rem A  - dollars spent on the team
    TurnNo      As Number       Rem D3 - fortnights on the trail
    Eating      As Number       Rem E  - 1 poorly / 2 moderately / 3 well
    Skill       As Number       Rem D9 - 1 ace .. 5 shaky (0 for braggarts)
    Injured     As Boolean      Rem K8
    Ill         As Boolean      Rem S4
    ShowPass    As Boolean      Rem M9 - report 950 miles while backtracking
    ClearedPass As Boolean      Rem F1 - South Pass behind you
    ClearedBlue As Boolean      Rem F2 - Blue Mountains behind you
    FortDue     As Boolean      Rem X1 - a fort is reachable this turn
    Fate        As Outcome

Def NewTrail(oxen As Number, food As Number, ammo As Number, clothes As Number, misc As Number, skill As Number) As Trail
    Let cash = StartBudget() - oxen - food - ammo - clothes - misc
    Trail(0, 0, food, 50 * ammo, clothes, misc, cash, oxen, 0, 1, skill, False, False, False, False, False, False, Rolling())

Def IsRolling(t As Trail) As Boolean
    Select Case Fate(t)
        Case Rolling
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def Kill(t As Trail, msg As String) As Trail
    With(t, Fate = Dead(msg))

Def DiedOf(t As Trail) As String
    If Injured(t) Then
        "YOU DIED OF INJURIES"
    Else
        "YOU DIED OF PNEUMONIA"

Rem ---- the calendar --------------------------------------------------
Rem Each turn is a fortnight; the twentieth date is not on the list
Rem because nobody who needs it survives the winter.

Def TrailDates() As List Of String
    { "APRIL 12", "APRIL 26", "MAY 10", "MAY 24", "JUNE 7", "JUNE 21", "JULY 5", "JULY 19", "AUGUST 2", "AUGUST 16", "AUGUST 31", "SEPTEMBER 13", "SEPTEMBER 27", "OCTOBER 11", "OCTOBER 25", "NOVEMBER 8", "NOVEMBER 22", "DECEMBER 6", "DECEMBER 20" }

Def TurnDate(n As Number) As String
    "MONDAY " & Nth(TrailDates(), n) & " 1847"

Def OutOfTime(n As Number) As Boolean
    n >= 20

Rem ---- turn housekeeping ---------------------------------------------

Rem Supplies never go negative on the books, everything is whole by
Rem morning, and the odometer reading is remembered for the final turn.
Def ClampSupplies(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Floor(Max(0, Food(t))), Bullets = Floor(Max(0, Bullets(t))), Clothing = Floor(Max(0, Clothing(t))), Misc = Floor(Max(0, Misc(t))), Cash = Floor(Cash(t)), Miles = Floor(Miles(t)), PrevMiles = Floor(Miles(t)))

Def NeedsDoctor(t As Trail) As Boolean
    Ill(t) Or Injured(t)

Def PayDoctor(t As Trail) As Trail
    If Cash(t) < DoctorFee() Then
        Kill(With(t, Cash = 0), "YOU CAN'T AFFORD A DOCTOR\n" & DiedOf(t))
    Else
        With(t, Cash = Cash(t) - DoctorFee(), Ill = False, Injured = False)

Rem What the odometer claims: 950 while backtracking over South Pass.
Def ShownMiles(t As Trail) As Number
    If ShowPass(t) Then
        950
    Else
        Miles(t)

Rem ---- eating --------------------------------------------------------

Def MealCost(e As Number) As Number
    8 + 5 * e

Def CanEat(t As Trail, e As Number) As Boolean
    Food(t) >= MealCost(e)

Def Eat(t As Trail, e As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) - MealCost(e), Eating = e)

Def Starved(t As Trail) As Boolean
    Food(t) < LowFood()

Rem ---- travel --------------------------------------------------------
Rem A fortnight's progress: a better team goes further; r is in [0,1).

Def Travel(t As Trail, r As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) + 200 + (Oxen(t) - 220) / 5 + 10 * r)

Rem ---- the fort ------------------------------------------------------

Def BuyFood(t As Trail, p As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Cash = Cash(t) - p, Food = Food(t) + FortRate() * p)

Def BuyAmmo(t As Trail, p As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Cash = Cash(t) - p, Bullets = Floor(Bullets(t) + FortRate() * p * 50))

Def BuyClothes(t As Trail, p As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Cash = Cash(t) - p, Clothing = Clothing(t) + FortRate() * p)

Def BuyMisc(t As Trail, p As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Cash = Cash(t) - p, Misc = Misc(t) + FortRate() * p)

Rem Stopping anywhere costs the fortnight forty-five miles.
Def Detour(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 45)

Rem ---- shooting ------------------------------------------------------
Rem The console times how long the player took to type the word; quality
Rem is seconds over a two-second grace, eased by claimed inexperience
Rem (an ace gets no slack). Zero is a perfect shot, nine a ruined one.

Def ShotQuality(elapsedSecs As Number, matched As Boolean, skill As Number) As Number
    If Not matched Then
        MissShot()
    Else
        Max(0, elapsedSecs - 2 - (skill - 1))

Rem ---- hunting -------------------------------------------------------

Def CanHunt(t As Trail) As Boolean
    Bullets(t) > FewBullets()

Def BigKill(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) + 52 + Rnd() * 6, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 10 - Rnd() * 4)

Def GoodShot(t As Trail, b1 As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) + 48 - 2 * b1, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 10 - 3 * b1)

Def GameGotAway(b1 As Number, r As Number) As Boolean
    100 + r < 13 * b1

Rem ---- riders --------------------------------------------------------
Rem The chance of riders peaks around the 400-mile mark; r in [0,1).

Def RidersApproach(m As Number, r As Number) As Boolean
    r * 10 <= ((m / 100 - 4) ^ 2 + 72) / ((m / 100 - 4) ^ 2 + 12) - 1

Rem Looks deceive one time in five.
Def ActualMood(lookFriendly As Boolean, r As Number) As Boolean
    If r <= 0.2 Then
        Not lookFriendly
    Else
        lookFriendly

Def FriendlyRun(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) + 15, Oxen = Oxen(t) - 10)

Def FriendlyAttack(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 5, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 100)

Def FriendlyCircle(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 20)

Def HostileRun(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) + 20, Misc = Misc(t) - 15, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 150, Oxen = Oxen(t) - 40)

Def HostileShootout(t As Trail, b1 As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Bullets = Bullets(t) - b1 * 40 - 80)

Def HostileCircle(t As Trail, b1 As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Bullets = Bullets(t) - b1 * 30 - 80, Miles = Miles(t) - 25)

Rem Continuing past hostiles who attack anyway.
Def RidersSneak(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 150, Misc = Misc(t) - 15)

Def Knifed(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Injured = True)

Def Massacred(t As Trail) As Boolean
    Bullets(t) < 0

Rem ---- the misfortune table ------------------------------------------
Rem The DATA statement of line 3620: a roll of 100*Rnd lands on the
Rem first level it does not exceed; past them all is event 16, the one
Rem good thing that can happen on the trail.

Def EventLevels() As List Of Number
    { 6, 11, 13, 15, 17, 22, 32, 35, 37, 42, 44, 54, 64, 69, 95 }

Def PickFrom(levels As List Of Number, r As Number, k As Number) As Number
    If IsEmpty(levels) Then
        k
    Else
        If r <= First(levels) Then
            k
        Else
            PickFrom(Rest(levels), r, k + 1)

Def PickEvent(r As Number) As Number
    PickFrom(EventLevels(), r, 1)

Def WagonBreaks(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 15 - 5 * Rnd(), Misc = Misc(t) - 8)

Def OxLeg(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 25, Oxen = Oxen(t) - 20)

Def BrokenArm(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 5 - 4 * Rnd(), Misc = Misc(t) - 2 - 3 * Rnd())

Def OxWanders(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 17)

Def SonLost(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 10)

Def UnsafeWater(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 10 * Rnd() - 2)

Def HeavyRains(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) - 10, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 500, Misc = Misc(t) - 15, Miles = Miles(t) - 10 * Rnd() - 5)

Def BanditsShoot(t As Trail, b1 As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 20 * b1)

Def BanditsRob(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Cash = Cash(t) / 3)

Def BanditsWound(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(Knifed(t), Misc = Misc(t) - 5, Oxen = Oxen(t) - 20)

Def WagonFire(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) - 40, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 400, Misc = Misc(t) - Rnd() * 8 - 3, Miles = Miles(t) - 15)

Def HeavyFog(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 10 - 5 * Rnd())

Def Snakebite(t As Trail) As Trail
    Let bit = With(t, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 10, Misc = Misc(t) - 5)
    If Misc(bit) < 0 Then
        Kill(bit, "YOU DIE OF SNAKEBITE SINCE YOU HAVE NO MEDICINE")
    Else
        bit

Def SwampedWagon(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) - 30, Clothing = Clothing(t) - 20, Miles = Miles(t) - 20 - 20 * Rnd())

Def WolvesLoot(t As Trail, b1 As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 20 * b1, Clothing = Clothing(t) - b1 * 4, Food = Food(t) - b1 * 8)

Def HailStorm(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 5 - Rnd() * 10, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 200, Misc = Misc(t) - 4 - Rnd() * 3)

Rem Cold snap past the 950-mile mark: warm enough or ill.
Def ClothesEnough(c As Number, r As Number) As Boolean
    c > 22 + 4 * r

Rem Whether careless eating catches up with you (event 15): poor eaters
Rem always sicken, moderate ones usually, hearty ones half the time.
Def IllnessDue(e As Number, r As Number) As Boolean
    Select Case e
        Case 1
            True
        Case 2
            r > 0.25
        Case Else
            r < 0.5

Def HelpfulIndians(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) + 14)

Rem ---- illness -------------------------------------------------------
Rem 1 wild, 2 bad, 3 serious; how you have been eating shifts the odds.
Rem Two independent rolls, both in [0,1).

Def IllKind(e As Number, r1 As Number, r2 As Number) As Number
    If 100 * r1 < 10 + 35 * (e - 1) Then
        1
    Else
        If 100 * r2 < 100 - 40 / 4 ^ (e - 1) Then
            2
        Else
            3

Def Illness(t As Trail, kind As Number) As Trail
    Let sick = TakeIll(t, kind)
    If Misc(sick) < 0 Then
        Kill(sick, "YOU RAN OUT OF MEDICAL SUPPLIES\n" & DiedOf(sick))
    Else
        sick

Def TakeIll(t As Trail, kind As Number) As Trail
    Select Case kind
        Case 1
            With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 5, Misc = Misc(t) - 2)
        Case 2
            With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 5, Misc = Misc(t) - 5)
        Case Else
            With(t, Misc = Misc(t) - 10, Ill = True)

Rem ---- mountains -----------------------------------------------------

Def InMountains(m As Number) As Boolean
    m > 950

Def RoughGoing(m As Number, r As Number) As Boolean
    r * 10 <= 9 - ((m / 100 - 15) ^ 2 + 72) / ((m / 100 - 15) ^ 2 + 12)

Def GetLost(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 60)

Def WagonDamage(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Misc = Misc(t) - 5, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 200, Miles = Miles(t) - 20 - 30 * Rnd())

Def SlowGoing(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Miles = Miles(t) - 45 - 50 * Rnd())

Def PassSnowed(r As Number) As Boolean
    r < 0.8

Def BlueSnowed(r As Number) As Boolean
    r < 0.7

Def MarkPass(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, ClearedPass = True)

Def MarkBlue(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, ClearedBlue = True)

Def Blizzard(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) - 25, Misc = Misc(t) - 10, Bullets = Bullets(t) - 300, Miles = Miles(t) - 30 - 40 * Rnd())

Def ColdInBlizzard(c As Number, r As Number) As Boolean
    c < 18 + 2 * r

Rem Driven back below the 950-mile mark, the odometer saves face.
Def CheckPass(t As Trail) As Trail
    If Miles(t) > 950 Then
        t
    Else
        With(t, ShowPass = True)

Rem ---- arrival -------------------------------------------------------
Rem The last fortnight is only partly used: the fraction of it spent on
Rem the trail fixes the day of the week and the date, and the unused
Rem days' rations come back.

Def ArrivalFraction(m2 As Number, m As Number) As Number
    (TotalMiles() - m2) / (m - m2)

Def ArrivalFood(t As Trail, frac As Number) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Food(t) + (1 - frac) * MealCost(Eating(t)))

Def WeekdayNames() As List Of String
    { "MONDAY", "TUESDAY", "WEDNESDAY", "THURSDAY", "FRIDAY", "SATURDAY", "SUNDAY" }

Def WeekdayName(frac As Number) As String
    Let f9 = Floor(frac * 14) + 1
    If f9 >= 8 Then
        Nth(WeekdayNames(), f9 - 7)
    Else
        Nth(WeekdayNames(), f9)

Rem Days since the March 29 start, counted in printed dates.
Def ArrivalDays(turnNo As Number, frac As Number) As Number
    turnNo * 14 + Floor(frac * 14)

Def ArrivalDate(days As Number) As String
    Select Case days
        Case <= 124
            "JULY " & Str(days - 93) & " 1847"
        Case <= 155
            "AUGUST " & Str(days - 124) & " 1847"
        Case <= 185
            "SEPTEMBER " & Str(days - 155) & " 1847"
        Case <= 216
            "OCTOBER " & Str(days - 185) & " 1847"
        Case <= 246
            "NOVEMBER " & Str(days - 216) & " 1847"
        Case Else
            "DECEMBER " & Str(days - 246) & " 1847"

Rem Nothing arrives in Oregon City owing money to the ledger.
Def ClampFinal(t As Trail) As Trail
    With(t, Food = Max(0, Food(t)), Bullets = Max(0, Bullets(t)), Clothing = Max(0, Clothing(t)), Misc = Max(0, Misc(t)), Cash = Max(0, Cash(t)))
